    "short_description": "The Tunisia Africa Business Council (TABC) is a non-governmental organization established in 2015 to promote economic integration, trade, and investment between Tunisia and Africa. Founded by prominent Tunisian business leaders, TABC aims to enhance South-South cooperation and create a sustainable development hub in Africa, with a focus on supporting Tunisian companies in their internationalization efforts.\n\nTABC offers a range of services, including business matchmaking, market access support, and strategic advisory. It organizes events like the Financing Investment and Trade in Africa (FITA) to strengthen Tunisia's presence in African markets. The organization also collaborates with various partners, including the Agency of the Promotion of Industry and Innovation (APII) and Afreximbank, to facilitate trade finance and support Tunisian exports. TABC serves Tunisian entrepreneurs, African investors, government officials, and financial institutions, positioning itself as a key player in fostering economic growth and cooperation across the continent.",
